s'oi

mihe t'omys

That is about the extent of my lojban.

I look forward to exploring this language.

I have interests in linguistics and grammars, as well as philisophy and
theology. I am wondering if so many questions are malformed or rendered
meaningless from a logical positivism standpoint due to the limitations of
the language.

I hope that learning lojban will help me organize some of my thinking, both
in lojban and English.

I also am studying Koine Greek at this time, so that I hope to have my own
Sapir-Whorf experience.

Thanks,
t'omys

